# 10. PLAYER STATE

Attributes represent ability.

State represents current condition.

Each player also has:

```text
fitness            0–100
match_sharpness    0–100
fatigue             0–100
morale              0–100
confidence          0–100
happiness           0–100
form                 dynamic
```

A world-class player at 65% physical condition should not perform like a fully fit world-class player.

---

# 11. PLAYER PERFORMANCE MODEL

Effective ability:

```text
effective_attribute =
base_attribute
× fitness_modifier
× fatigue_modifier
× morale_modifier
× confidence_modifier
× familiarity_modifier
```

Modifiers must remain fairly subtle.

Morale should matter without converting mediocre players into superstars.

Example bounds:

```text
Morale:
0.94 – 1.04

Fitness:
0.65 – 1.00

Fatigue:
0.82 – 1.00
```

---

# 12. PLAYER DEVELOPMENT

Development should occur continuously.

Concept:

```text
development_points =
age_curve
× professionalism
× coaching_quality
× facility_quality
× training_quality
× playing_time
× competition_quality
× morale
× potential_gap
× random_variation
```

Potential gap:

```text
potential_ceiling - current_ability
```

The smaller the gap becomes, the harder improvement becomes.

---

# 13. DEVELOPMENT AGE CURVES

General guideline:

```text
15–17    very rapid potential
18–20    rapid
21–23    strong
24–26    moderate
27–29    limited
30+      decline increasingly likely
```

Different attributes follow separate curves.

Physical:

```text
peak earlier
decline earlier
```

Mental:

```text
develop longer
decline slowly
```

Technical:

```text
middle
```

Goalkeeping:

```text
later development
later peak
```

