# 24. PLAYER DECISION ENGINE

A player evaluates candidate actions.

Example:

```text
PASS
DRIBBLE
SHOOT
CROSS
CLEAR
HOLD
RECYCLE
THROUGH_BALL
```

Each candidate receives:

```text
utility(action) =
technical_score
+ spatial_score
+ tactical_score
+ mental_score
+ player_trait_score
+ game_context_score
- risk_score
```

Then choose probabilistically.

Do not simply select maximum utility.

Use a softmax-like model.

This produces variation without pure randomness.

