3. Do not duplicate an existing system.
4. Never modify architecture merely to make one feature easier.
5. Do not put business logic in UI.
6. Do not disable failing tests.
7. Do not weaken assertions.
8. Do not replace deterministic behaviour with uncontrolled randomness.
9. Add tests for new behaviour.
10. Run applicable tests before completion.
11. Document database migrations.
12. Preserve backward-compatible saves where practical.
13. No placeholder implementation may be described as complete.
14. Do not silently catch exceptions.
15. Do not commit generated junk files.
