# 155. FINAL ARCHITECTURAL PRINCIPLE

The game should be capable of answering:

> Why did this happen?

If a player develops rapidly:

There should be a reason.

If an AI club signs someone:

There should be a reason.

If a striker misses repeatedly:

There should be measurable reasons.

If a club becomes wealthy:

The money should come from somewhere.

If a league becomes stronger:

Historical events should explain it.

If a team dominates:

Its players, manager, finances and tactics should explain it.

That causal consistency is what will separate Football Dynasty from a shallow AI-generated football manager.

**The world should not pretend to simulate football.**

**The world should actually simulate its own version of football.**
